# Which test suites use the shared framework, and which still carry a case
# runner of their own.
#
# tests/testlib.ps is the one place a case that may raise is run, and the
# one place that puts the world back afterwards. A suite asks for it with
# `%!testlib` on its first line; run-ps-test.sh prepends it to those and to
# nothing else, because some suites here assert that a program's own
# dictionary starts empty or count the dictionary stack, and six read their
# own colour_sampling_test.ps           refuses

